WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:16.772
Unit twenty-nine: Reflexive Pronouns (myself / yourself). Today you will talk about actions that return to the subject.

4
00:00:17.072 --> 00:00:19.504
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.816
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.616
Myself.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:30.149
Myself means me, when I am the doer and the receiver.

8
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.902
I cut myself.

9
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:35.215
Your turn. Say: Myself.

10
00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.161
Myself.

11
00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:40.941
Yourself.

12
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.320
Yourself means you, when you are the doer and the receiver.

13
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:47.057
Look at yourself.

14
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.035
Your turn. Say: Yourself.

15
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.889
Yourself.

16
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.616
Himself.

17
00:00:56.617 --> 00:00:59.800
Himself means him, when he is the doer and the receiver.

18
00:01:00.417 --> 00:01:01.627
He hurt himself.

19
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:04.811
Your turn. Say: Himself.

20
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.610
Himself.

21
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.316
Herself.

22
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:14.350
Herself means her, when she is the doer and the receiver.

23
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.311
She taught herself.

24
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:19.859
Your turn. Say: Herself.

25
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.608
Herself.

26
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.537
Ourselves.

27
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.583
Ourselves means us, when we are the doers and the receivers.

28
00:01:30.183 --> 00:01:31.753
We enjoyed ourselves.

29
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:35.002
Your turn. Say: Ourselves.

30
00:01:37.867 --> 00:01:39.216
Ourselves.

31
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.009
Themselves.

32
00:01:42.017 --> 00:01:45.467
Themselves means them, when they are the doers and the receivers.

33
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:47.549
They made it themselves.

34
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.162
Your turn. Say: Themselves.

35
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.570
Themselves.

36
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:57.480
Reflexive.

37
00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:00.843
Reflexive means returning to the subject.

38
00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.705
A reflexive pronoun ends in -self.

39
00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:07.224
Your turn. Say: Reflexive.

40
00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.091
Reflexive.

41
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:12.839
By myself.

42
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.337
By myself means alone, without help.

43
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.357
I did it by myself.

44
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.347
Your turn. Say: By myself.

45
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.271
By myself.

46
00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:29.752
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.838
Visal, did you cut yourself? What does the pronoun do?

48
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:50.199
Yourself shows that you did the action and you received it. A reflexive pronoun ends in -self or -selves: myself, yourself, himself, herself, itself, ourselves, yourselves, themselves.

49
00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:52.482
When do we use them?

50
00:02:53.583 --> 00:03:06.318
When the subject and the object are the same: She looked at herself. I taught myself. We also use them for emphasis: I made it myself. By myself means alone.

51
00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:09.242
Are there verbs that do not need them?

52
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:24.487
Yes. We do not say I washed myself every day in English if the meaning is clear; we say I washed. Also do not use them after prepositions of place: Put it behind you, not behind yourself.

53
00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:27.018
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:27.883 --> 00:03:32.785
Grammar focus: Reflexive pronouns: myself and yourself and himself ….

55
00:03:33.085 --> 00:03:34.272
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:36.217
I cut myself.

57
00:03:37.117 --> 00:03:38.849
She taught herself English.

58
00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.274
We enjoyed ourselves.

59
00:03:42.233 --> 00:03:50.644
Use myself, yourself, himself, herself, itself, ourselves, yourselves or themselves when the subject and object are the same person. By myself means alone.

60
00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:54.779
Be careful! Don't say: I hurt me yesterday.

61
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:58.803
Say: I hurt myself yesterday.

62
00:03:59.103 --> 00:04:02.124
Use myself when subject and object are the same.

63
00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:05.435
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:06.233 --> 00:04:07.362
Doing It Yourself.

65
00:04:07.662 --> 00:04:09.917
I cut myself while I was cooking.

66
00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:13.212
My sister taught herself to play the guitar.

67
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.118
We enjoyed ourselves at the party.

68
00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:19.156
They built the house themselves.

69
00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.015
I did my homework by myself.

70
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.241
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:29.735
She looked at blank in the mirror.

72
00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:33.316
A, her. B, herself. C, she.

73
00:04:36.867 --> 00:04:38.727
The answer is B: herself.

74
00:04:39.883 --> 00:04:41.604
We enjoyed blank at the party.

75
00:04:41.904 --> 00:04:44.966
A, us. B, ourselves. C, we.

76
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.453
The answer is B: ourselves.

77
00:04:51.617 --> 00:04:54.199
He made the cake blank. (he did it alone)

78
00:04:54.499 --> 00:04:57.723
A, himself. B, him. C, his.

79
00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.220
The answer is A: himself.

80
00:05:04.383 --> 00:05:05.953
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:06.253 --> 00:05:10.255
A, I hurt me.. B, I hurt myself.. C, I hurt mine..

82
00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.194
The answer is B: I hurt myself..

83
00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.371
According to the reading, who taught herself to play the guitar?

84
00:05:20.671 --> 00:05:24.406
A, my sister. B, my friend. C, my mother.

85
00:05:27.967 --> 00:05:30.036
The answer is A: my sister.

86
00:05:31.233 --> 00:05:34.513
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.640
Write a sentence using 'myself' or 'yourself'.

88
00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.904
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:48.204 --> 00:05:58.896
I taught myself to cook. Please enjoy yourself at the party and look after yourself. I use myself when I am the subject and the object. I use yourself when I talk to you.

90
00:05:59.196 --> 00:06:00.928
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:01.817 --> 00:06:08.486
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reflexive pronouns: myself and yourself and himself ….

92
00:06:08.786 --> 00:06:13.377
Today's value is independence. Learn to do things by yourself, step by step.

93
00:06:13.677 --> 00:06:16.155
See you in Unit thirty. Goodbye!

94
00:06:16.455 --> 00:06:18.852
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

